review.notes:
Accepted after corrections. Independent review by Claude Code, session cc-c2c06b (issue #493). The blueprint was written by Claude Code cc-fb70e5 (PRs #3812, #3814, #3819, #3821). All 55 original nodes were checked against the sources, and every baseline citation against the pinned trees: 4 nodes were verified and 51 corrected, and 4 were added. The most serious correction: R25.5/weight-fourteen-at-eleven-is-a-twist was false. By Serre's recipe, a level-one ρ̄ at p = 11 whose inertia is a non-split extension with sub ω and quotient ω² has weight 14, and no twist of it has weight 2. Khare–Wintenberger's published Theorem 5.4 assumes p ≠ 11 for k = 14. The node now states the true dichotomy, and the small-weight theorem and table row 8 exclude (11, 14), a case no consumer uses (new source issue E9). The other substantive corrections:
- three degree-bound rows were weakened to what the stated certification proves;
- a false class-number step for ℚ(ζ₁₂) was replaced by Mathlib's discriminant criterion;
- an unjustified step in Schoof's case l = 7 failed for A₄ and was replaced by the units argument;
- poitouLowerBound_div_mono was false at n = 0;
- a hidden positive-definiteness step became a node;
- the 2-adic bound was misattributed to Tate;
- a false 'special to ℚ' acceptance was corrected;
- the definition of a simple 2-group scheme was missing 'nonzero';
- GL₂-type is now over a number field.
Requests: oddness moved to R01.4, the explicit formula to AN.4, Hilbert class fields to ClassFieldTheory Layer 13 and the local-global dictionary to NumberFieldArithmetic Layer 5. Requests were added to R01.6, R19.4, R19.5 and ProfiniteCohomology Layer 9. 38 baseline declarations were added: the existing Tau Ceti unit filtration, tame different exponent, isogenies, endomorphism ring, positive-definite API and Mathlib class-number criteria. Source issues E1–E4 were confirmed and E5–E11 added. The suggested file had 29 elaboration errors at the pinned baseline, a mis-parenthesised poitouLowerBound and Prop-valued placeholders that section 13 forbids. It now carries every packet name and elaborates against Mathlib 082e2d3 and Tau Ceti f790474 with only the expected placeholder-proof warnings; 12 declarations whose conditions cannot yet be stated are recorded in its header. check_blueprint --index: 0 errors, 0 warnings. The roadmap document (readmes/) is outside this review and still states several corrected claims; see the review report.
